@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Franchise changes observed in completed trades
+
+This extends the existing Franchise History summary, season coverage and trade follow-through. It does not create a second history pipeline, roster inventory or analytical grade.
+
+## Confirmed customer gap and retained control
+
+On build 2249, the retained Day Traders source replay has two admitted completed trades for source roster 4 in the 2026 source season. Direct original consideration contains one player acquisition, three player disposals, five exact pick acquisitions and two exact pick disposals. The existing summary showed only trade counts and first-round picks, requiring manual reconstruction for other movements. Arkham's bounded replay does not establish a completed-trade sample for the selected franchise: its counts remain unknown. These are partial retained captures, not new production measurements or exhaustive league coverage.
+
+## Contract
+
+The existing canonical directed-movement reader admits consideration independently for players and exact picks. Each completed transaction is counted once per source league/transaction identity. Conflicting versions, malformed transactions, pending/rejected/cancelled/failed records, waivers, corrections and unlinked franchise observations do not become completed trade activity. A repeated asset in two real deals appears in both gross directions; net is only acquisitions minus disposals **in the observed trade sample**, never current holdings or complete franchise progress. Incomplete consideration preserves supported lower bounds and withholds the affected net. An observed pick conversion remains a draft event, not an additional trade acquisition.
+
+Source-season selection uses retained authoritative season identities. It is not a guessed date range; supported completion dates describe only the dated subset. Missing periods remain unknown. A zero for an empty selected period requires complete source coverage and supported franchise continuity. Known zero transfers within an observed nonempty sample do not establish zero activity in unacquired periods. A source version change withholds every numeric summary.
+
+Exact pick identities retain draft year, round and original source roster. “Own” refers to that original franchise in the source-linked chain, not today's owner or a manager's tenure. Historical event labels reuse source-season identities. Existing subsequent-trade, package, pick-conversion and contextual Back paths are retained. Manager changes remain season observations and are not backdated to transaction actors. Current values, projections and ownership are not used to supply historical facts.
+
+## Bounds and preservation
+
+This reuses already retained transaction and identity reads, their existing 100,000-row boundary and coherence token. It adds no provider calls, publication, source store, runtime owner or page-triggered analysis. At most 256 exact asset details and four supporting links per identity are retained for the request; counts include the full admitted bounded sample, with truncation disclosed. The existing 12-deal sample links, event pagination and season coverage remain available. Rendering disclosures causes no evaluation or acquisition.
+
+Beginning/end roster and capital inventories are explicitly not established by these transaction observations. Waivers, drafts and drops remain separately visible in the factual timeline. FOIS remains RETAINED / NOT REVALIDATED. Sleeper projection/results authority, Market/Custom formulas, Trade verdicts, saved settings, account isolation, submitted lineups, scoring and all memory/admission policies are unchanged.
+
+## Acceptance and publication
+
+Final validation must use the exact candidate commit/tree: focused controls, rendered phone journeys (320×432, 375×667, 390×844 and desktop), complete canonical regression/all ten gates, and all required hosted jobs. Keyboard/touch browser emulation does not establish physical iPhone/Safari acceptance. Source replay, disposable fixtures and fresh authorized live observations must be reported separately. No full-suite result or deployment is claimed by this design record.
